From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mindone <mindone@localhost>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] telephony: add config_powerOffRadioWhenNoActiveSubscription

A device may want to switch off the cellular radio of a logical modem
while that modem has no usable subscription: the slot is empty, the card
is unusable, or the user turned the SIM off with "Use SIM" (uicc
applications disabled). The modem then cannot register and, depending on
the network, can keep searching for an acceptable cell indefinitely.

The flag is read by frameworks/opt/telephony
NoSubscriptionRadioPowerController. It defaults to false, so behaviour
does not change unless a device overlay enables it. Emergency calls keep
working: they power the radio on through the existing forEmergencyCall
path, which clears every radio-off reason, exactly as in airplane mode.

---
diff --git a/core/res/res/values/config_telephony.xml b/core/res/res/values/config_telephony.xml
index da464012..d703b4da 100644
--- a/core/res/res/values/config_telephony.xml
+++ b/core/res/res/values/config_telephony.xml
@@ -52,6 +52,9 @@
     <integer name="config_delay_for_ims_dereg_millis">0</integer>
     <java-symbol type="integer" name="config_delay_for_ims_dereg_millis" />
 
+    <bool name="config_powerOffRadioWhenNoActiveSubscription">false</bool>
+    <java-symbol type="bool" name="config_powerOffRadioWhenNoActiveSubscription" />
+
     <!-- Define the bar of considering the availability of a subscription is stable in milliseconds,
          where 0 means immediate switch, and negative milliseconds indicates the auto data switch
          feature is disabled.-->
-- 
2.50.1

